X', 'date': '2020-07-28 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Quest Diagnostics Says During Past Week Surpassed 9.2 Mln Covid-19 Molecular Diagnostic Test Results Delivered To Date', 'text': 'DURING THE PAST WEEK SURPASSED 9.2 MILLION COVID-19 MOLECULAR DIAGNOSTIC TEST RESULTS DELIVERED TO DATE.CURRENTLY HAVE CAPACITY TO PERFORM AS MANY AS 135,000 MOLECULAR DIAGNOSTIC TESTS A DAY.WORKING TO INCREASE CAPACITY TO 150,000 COVID-19 MOLECULAR DIAGNOSTIC TESTS A DAY BY NEXT WEEK.DURING THE PAST WEEK, SAW TEST CAPACITY SLIGHTLY EXCEED DEMAND FOR THE FIRST TIME SINCE EARLY JUNE.MOST SIGNIFICANT HURDLE CO FACES NOW IS LIMITS TO COMPLEX TESTING PLATFORMS & CHEMICAL REAGENTS REQUIRED TO PERFORM TESTING.EXPECT AS CAPACITY GROWS, WILL BE ABLE TO RETURN TO AVERAGE TURNAROUND TIMES IN RANGE OF 1 DAY FOR PRIORITY 1 PATIENTS.AVERAGE TURNAROUND TIME FOR REPORTING TEST RESULTS IS NOW OVER TWO DAYS FOR PRIORITY 1 PATIENTS & 7 DAYS FOR ALL OTHER PATIENTS.RATE OF INCOMING SPECIMENS INTO OUR LABORATORIES HAS HELD STEADY OVER APPROXIMATELY PAST 2 WEEKS.EXPECT AS CAPACITY GROWS, WILL BE ABLE TO RETURN TO AVERAGE TURNAROUND TIME OF ABOUT 3 DAYS FOR MOST NON-PRIORITY 1 PATIENTS.HAVE STEADILY ADDED CAPACITY SINCE WE BEGAN TO PROVIDE SERVICES IN EARLY MARCH, BUT IT WILL TAKE TIME TO ADD MORE.'}{'symbol': 'RTX', 'date': '2020-07-28 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Raytheon Technologies CEO Says Remain Confident In Ability To Deliver On Synergy Targets, Which Is Over $1 Bln In Gross Savings', 'text': 'RAYTHEON TECHNOLOGIES CEO SAYS REMAIN CONFIDENT IN ABILITY TO DELIVER ON SYNERGY TARGETS, WHICH IS OVER $1 BILLION IN GROSS SAVINGS - CONF CALL.RAYTHEON TECHNOLOGIES CEO SAYS ON TRACK TO ACHIEVE $2 BILLION IN COST SAVINGS THIS YEAR & $4 BILLION IN CASH CONSERVATION ACTIONS BY END OF YEAR.RAYTHEON TECHNOLOGIES CEO - EFFECTS OF PANDEMIC ON ECONOMY, COMMERCIAL AEROSPACE PROVEN TO BE LOT WORSE THAN ORIGINALLY PROJECTED EVEN FEW MONTHS AGO.RAYTHEON TECHNOLOGIES CEO SAYS NOW WOULD EXPECT IT WILL TAKE AT LEAST UNTIL 2023 F